    "overview": "<p>Things are getting interesting! <b>Mcginning to believe</b> remains top of the pile, but the gap is closing, with <b>DuncanDisorder</b> putting in the highest score of the week with an impressive <b>116 points</b> to climb from 7th to 2nd. <b>MattyCashInTheAttic</b> also moved up to 3rd, while <b>Livesdownthelaine</b> jumped into 4th. There was a tougher week for <b>Redder's Rejects</b>, dropping from 2nd to 11th after managing just 70 points. At the other end, <b>Dragospear’s XI</b> made the biggest move upwards, climbing a massive ten places to 12th, while a very poor week for <b>Mcginniesta</b> sees them rooted to the bottom on 80 points. With just 33 points separating 2nd to 10th, things are already looking very tight behind the leader.</p><p>The Premier League certainly served up another entertaining weekend. <b>Haaland finally exploded into life with two goals</b> as Man City thrashed Crystal Palace 4-1, while <b>Bruno Fernandes went from blanking in GW1 to scoring a hat-trick</b> in Man United's 5-2 comeback against Ipswich - a pretty good reminder of why selling either of them after one blank might be a bit premature! Chelsea continued their perfect start with a crazy <b>4-3 win over Brighton</b>, while Arsenal made it two wins from two with a 1-0 victory at Villa. Meanwhile, Spurs are already bottom after another defeat, this time 2-0 to Newcastle.</p><p><b>Two weeks down, and already plenty of twists and turns - both on the pitch and in our league.</b></p>",
